  "body": "Maintainer request from #1452 (\"We should be able to load DXF file to do profile cuts on.\").\n\nDepends on #1864.\n\n## Goal\nAdd open-chain centerline machining to `machining2d::trace` and connect both `Engrave` and `Trace` to open and closed DXF sketch chains and layers.\n\n## Scope\n- Extend `machining2d::trace` and `OpParams::Engrave` / `OpParams::Trace` (`crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs`, lines 1749-1815) so they machine both open polylines (`Vec<Point2>`) and closed `Region` loops along tool centerline without requiring a closed boundary area.\n- Update `crates/app/src/operation/selection.rs` so `Engrave` and `Trace` accept open DXF sketch chains and layers (removing the closed-loop-only block for those two centerline operations).\n- Keep existing `Mode::Engrave` verify semantics and check crossing, stock-rapid, and fixture laws against setup stock (`part_solid = false`).\n- Preserve true arcs on curved DXF centerline segments and support depth stepping cleanly via `Location` and setup alignment.\n\n## Done means\n`Engrave` and `Trace` generate verified multi-pass or single-pass centerline toolpaths and golden CL on both open DXF strokes and closed loops without a 3D mesh; open strokes no longer fail with a closed-region refusal; `.camproj` round-trip and MCP tests pass.\n\nPart of #1452\n",
